    "title": "Dallas Mavericks TV Schedule",
    "text": "Mark your calendars for #1 pick Cooper Flagg and the Dallas Mavericks with the following local and national TV schedule. (Full NBA schedule available here.) This site may earn a commission on subscriptions purchased via this page. No upcoming games scheduled.Past GamesSunday, April 12, 2026 TimeGame / TV8:30 pmChicago Bulls vs Dallas MavericksNBA League Pass | A CHSN | H KFAA Friday, April 10, 2026 TimeGame / TV8:00 pmDallas Mavericks vs San Antonio SpursNBA League Pass | A KFAA, WFAA | H KENS Wednesday, April 8, 2026 TimeGame / TV10:00 pmDallas Mavericks vs Phoenix SunsNBA League Pass | A KFAA | H KTVK, KPHE Tuesday, April 7, 2026 TimeGame / TV10:30 pmDallas Mavericks vs Los Angeles ClippersNBA League Pass | A KFAA | H FDSN SC | NBA TV Canada Sunday, April 5, 2026 TimeGame / TV7:30 pmSunday Night BasketballLos Angeles Lakers vs Dallas MavericksNBC, Peacock, Telemundo | CTV2, TSN Friday, April 3, 2026 TimeGame / TV8:30 pmOrlando Magic vs Dallas MavericksNBA League Pass | A FDSN FL, WESH | H KFAA Tuesday, March 31, 2026 TimeGame / TV8:00 pmDallas Mavericks vs Milwaukee BucksNBA League Pass | A KFAA | H FDSN WI How to Watch Mavericks Games The Mavericks followed up an NBA Finals appearance in 2024 with one of the most dramatic regular seasons in memory the following year, trading Luka Doncic at midseason and ultimately missing the playoffs. But that bad fortune resulted in Dallas winning the #1 pick in the draft and selecting Cooper Flagg, who joins a playoff ready roster that includes Anthony Davis and — eventually — the currently-injured Kyrie Irving. Dallas is set for 26 nationally televised games this season, including eight on ESPN/ABC (highlighted by a Christmas Day matchup with the Warriors), ten on NBC Sports (including two Peacock exclusives), five on Prime Video and three on NBA TV. Locally, the Mavericks will again play their games on local over-the-air affiliates in the Dallas area. Independent affiliate KFAA is set to carry 65 games this season, including seven that are simulcast on ABC affiliate WFAA (not counting the national ABC games that will also air on that affiliate). Those games are also available to stream direct-to-subscriber through MavsTV. Viewing options presented below: Oct 6, 2025; Fort Worth, Texas, USA; Dallas Mavericks forward Cooper Flagg (32) is interviewed after the game against the Oklahoma City Thunder during the second half at Dickie’s Arena. Mandatory Credit: Jerome Miron-Imagn Images Direct-to-Subscriber Platforms Local games (MavsTV): MavsTV (in-market only): Local Mavericks games can be streamed for $15/mo through MavsTV or $125 for the full season. NBA League Pass (out-of-market only): All out-of-market locally televised games, plus NBA TV. Also available as a standalone purchase through Amazon Prime Video. National games (ESPN/ABC, NBC/Peacock and Prime Video): Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Amazon Prime Video: All Amazon-produced games on Prime Video, plus the ability to purchase NBA League Pass as an add-on. Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Does not include KFAA. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $100 off YouTube TV ($20 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3); NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC, the NBC broadcast network and KFAA/WFAA. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC, the NBC broadcast network and KFAA/WFAA; NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC, the NBC broadcast network and KFAA/WFAA. Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Does not include KFAA. In-Person See the Mavericks in person at the American Airlines Center, or catch them on the road, by purchasing tickets from Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime. No Result View All Result © 2026 Jon Lewis, Sports Media Watch",
